              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "The length of a rectangle is increased by 60% but its area remains the same.",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "break"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "By what percentage is the width decreased?",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$37.5\\%$ decrease.",
          "worked": "Let $d$ be the width multiplier. Since area is length × width and remains unchanged,\n$$\\begin{align*}1.6d&=1\\\\d&=\\frac{1}{1.6}\\\\d&=0.625\\end{align*}$$\nThe width is $62.5\\%$ of its original value, so the decrease is $100\\%-62.5\\%=37.5\\%$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      },
      {
        "id": "p50-q5-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": {
          "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
          "version": 1,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "id": "p50-q5-b-prompt",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "left",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 2,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "The length of another rectangle is decreased by 25% and its area remains the same.",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "break"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "By what percentage is the width increased?",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$33.33\\dot{3}\\%$ increase.",
          "worked": "Let $d$ be the width multiplier. Since area is length × width and remains unchanged,\n$$\\begin{align*}0.75d&=1\\\\d&=\\frac{1}{0.75}\\\\d&=\\frac{4}{3}\\end{align*}$$\nThe fractional increase in width is $\\frac{4}{3}-1=\\frac{1}{3}$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Percentage increase}&=\\frac{1}{3}\\times100\\%\\\\&=33.33\\dot{3}\\%\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46
      }
    ]
  },
